# Dashboard redesign + motion

When redesigning or adding dashboard pages/forms, keep this visual and motion language.

## Visual system

- **Hero**: green gradient (`from-brand-deep via-[#0a4a10] to-brand-primary`), soft blur orb, eyebrow + title + short description. Use `PageHero` from `components/dashboard/page-shell.tsx`.
- **Sections**: stepped cards (`01` / `02` / …) with `from-brand-tint/50` header strip. Use `FormSection`.
- **Live preview**: sticky right column with same green hero + summary tiles (stores, users, profile).
- **Actions**: sticky bottom bar (`StickyFormActions`) — not a lonely footer button.
- **Surfaces**: `rounded-2xl`, `border-border/80`, light shadow — match Stores / Site settings / Role pages.
- Prefer **Store / Users / Profile** naming in UI copy (not “shop” for vendor stores).

## Motion (Framer Motion — keep memory low)

- Dependency: `framer-motion`. Wrap dashboard in `MotionProvider` (`LazyMotion` + `domAnimation` only).
- Import `FadeUp`, `FadeIn`, `Stagger`, `StaggerItem`, or `m` from `components/motion.tsx`.
- Shared presets live in `lib/motion.ts` (`fadeUp`, `fadeIn`, stagger). Do not invent new spring/layout animations per page.
- **Do**: opacity + small `translateY` (~10–12px), short duration (~0.28–0.35s), stagger children lightly.
- **Do not**: `layout` animations, drag/gestures, AnimatePresence on large tables, full `motion` import (use LazyMotion `m`), heavy parallax, infinite loops.
- Always go through `useMotionSafe()` so `prefers-reduced-motion` disables movement.

## Forms

- Create/edit mutating forms: shadcn Form + react-hook-form + zodResolver + safe-input (see form-upload-security rule).
- Profile / user / store edit pages should use the page-shell section pattern above.
